course: dictionary
lesson: 10829
title: Words with a place inside them
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. Venetian is one of them. It is about Venice, a city in Italy. Once you know that, many sentences make more sense.
explain: Venice is built on water, with canals instead of streets, so people travel by boat. «Venetian» can describe a thing from Venice, like «Venetian glass», or a person from there, like «a Venetian merchant», who is a trader from Venice.
explain: Use the clues around the word to work out which meaning fits. In «a Venetian merchant called Marco Polo», the word is describing where the merchant came from. Read the words around it first, then check your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Venetian means from or to do with Venice, a city in Italy.
fact: A Venetian is a person who comes from Venice.
fact: Venice is built on water, with canals instead of streets.
fact: Venetian glass and Venetian masks are famous art from Venice.
fact: A venetian blind is a window blind made of many thin flat strips that tilt to let light in or keep it out.
exercise: «Genghis's grandson Kublai Khan became emperor of China, and a Venetian merchant called Marco Polo wrote a book about his court.» Where did Marco Polo come from? | A small village in Spain | Rome | *Venice | China
exercise: A venetian blind has many thin flat strips. What do the strips do? | They hold up the roof of the house | *They tilt to let light in or keep it out | They turn into a boat at night | They make a loud noise when the wind blows
exercise: Venetian glass is famous. What does Venetian tell you about the glass? | *It was made in or is from Venice | It was made of wood from a forest | It was made in a school by children | It is always blue in colour
test: «Marco Polo was a Venetian merchant who wrote a famous book.» What does Venetian tell you about Marco Polo? | *He came from Venice | He lived on a ship all his life | He came from Vienna, a city in Austria | He was a king of Italy
test: Venice is built on what? | Ice, with snow instead of roads | Grass, with no roads at all | Sand, with camels instead of cars | *Water, with canals instead of streets
exam: A venetian blind has strips that tilt. What can you do with them? | Use them to make a boat for the canal | *Tilt them to let light in or keep it out | Paint them every day to make a picture | Fold them into paper planes
